former Egyptian President Hosni Mubarak  has died at the age of 91 Mubarak came  to power in the early 1980s and ruled  Egypt for three decades during that time  he forged stronger ties with the United  States and Israel while crushing  opposition at home that was until 2011  when he was ousted from power during the  Arab Spring  after more than 1 million Egyptians  angry about poverty and repression  called for him to go he ceded control to  the military he served time in prison  but his conviction was later overturned  I say yet Baba it was one last triumph  for Hosni Mubarak Egypt's former  president was acquitted after a trial  that lasted years the judges found him  innocent of involvement in the killing  of protesters during the 2011 Arab  Spring uprising that ended his 30-year  rule his career ended with a revolution  it began with an assassination in  October 1981 at a military parade  Islamist militants shot and killed then  President Anwar Sadat Mubarak the Vice  President escaped with minor injuries  and took over the presidency in the same  year he implemented emergency laws as  part of his battle against militants he  also expanded police powers in another  of his first moves he told the u.s. he  would stick by his country's 1979 peace  agreement with Israel the first by any  Arab nation Mubarak became an important  mediator between Israel and the  Palestinians for three decades he was  seen as a guarantor of stability in the  Middle East in return his country was  given billions of dollars in aid from  the US he was courted in Europe and  respected by his Raley's and Arabs alike  but at home Mubarak showed a different  face he cracked down on Islamists after  they orchestrated attacks and threatened  his rule Egypt's democracy was little  more than a facade all elections were  rigged  Mubarak did little to address the  poverty afflicting millions of Egyptians  as his inner circle and his own family  became wealthy as Egyptians resentment  grew and mass demonstrations broke out  Mubarak reacted with force when that  failed to curb the protests he attempted  to make concessions but in the end the  might of the Arab masses forced him to  step down Mubarak was put on trial in  jailed for six years mostly spent in a  military prison having served his  sentence for corruption the former  president was released and returned home  to his villa one of many properties  owned by his family his wife and sons  administered the assets accumulated  during his time in office  Mubarak ruled Egypt for 30 years honored  and feared in equal measure
 

